PR sketch: lightweight session labels spike

Summary
- Adds a minimal live-session label layer to zmx.
- Labels are key=value string pairs attached to the running session daemon.
- Intended for humans and tools/agents to identify and select sessions without encoding everything into the session name.
- Naming follows Kubernetes label conventions: labels are for selection/identification, not arbitrary metadata.

What this spike adds
- New IPC tags:
  - LabelGet
  - LabelSet
  - LabelUnset
  - LabelClear
  - LabelData
- New CLI surface:
  - zmx label get [session]
  - zmx label set [session] k=v ...
  - zmx label unset [session] key ...
  - zmx label clear [session]
- Session resolution behavior:
  - if no session argument is given, resolve from ZMX_SESSION
  - if session argument is ".", also resolve from ZMX_SESSION
- Daemon-side in-memory label map for each live session.

Intended UX
- From inside a zmx-managed shell:
  - zmx label set . status=busy project=jbang
  - zmx label get .
  - zmx label unset . status
- From outside:
  - zmx label set build-1 role=release target=homebrew

Why separate IPC tags
- Current ipc.Info is explicitly frozen in zmx.
- This spike avoids extending Info and instead uses additive tags for compatibility.

Current limitations / caveats
- This is a spike, not a finished patch.
- It was pushed without local compile/test on this host because zig is not installed here.
- Likely follow-up cleanup areas:
  - verify Zig API exactness for ArgIterator usage
  - verify StringHashMap ownership/update semantics
  - tighten CLI parsing edge cases
  - add help text/completions coverage cleanly
  - likely add list --labels and/or list --where in a follow-up instead of this first spike
- Labels are intentionally live-session scoped only, not persisted after session death.

Suggested next steps
1. Build and run locally with zig installed.
2. Fix any compile issues from the rough spike.
3. Decide whether to keep only label get/set/unset first and defer clear.
4. If the concept feels right, follow with:
   - zmx list --labels
   - zmx list --where key=value
   - attach/run-time label assignment

Intent
- Keep zmx small.
- Add just enough structure for session discovery and lightweight coordination.
- Avoid turning zmx into a workflow engine or state database.
